//fldigi macro definition file extended
// This file defines the macro structure(s) for the digital modem program, fldigi
// It also serves as a basis for any macros that are written by the user
//
// The top line of this file should always be the first line in every macro 
// definition file (.mdf) for the fldigi program to recognize it as such.
//

//
// Macro # 1
/$ 0 HD1 MT63-1KL @>|
<MODEM:MT63-1KL><GOFREQ:1500><TX>\n
HAM_DIGITAL_1: Infectious digital signals in the air\n
HAM_DIGITAL_1: Infectious digital signals in the air\n
HAM_DIGITAL_1: Infectious digital signals in the air\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 2
/$ 1 HD2 RTTY-45 @>|
<MODEM:RTTY><GOFREQ:1000><TX>\n
HAM_DIGITAL_2: NEON RAIN MAKES THIS WATERFALL GLOW\n
HAM_DIGITAL_2: NEON RAIN MAKES THIS WATERFALL GLOW\n
HAM_DIGITAL_2: NEON RAIN MAKES THIS WATERFALL GLOW\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 3
/$ 2 HD3 OLIVIA-4/250 @>|
<MODEM:OLIVIA-4/250><GOFREQ:2000><TX>\n
HAM_DIGITAL_3: Through the shadows and into the silicon\n
HAM_DIGITAL_3: Through the shadows and into the silicon\n
HAM_DIGITAL_3: Through the shadows and into the silicon\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 4
/$ 3 HD4 BPSK1000 @>|
<MODEM:BPSK1000><GOFREQ:1200><TX>\n
HAM_DIGITAL_4: The Rebels vanish undetected by the Empire\n
HAM_DIGITAL_4: The Rebels vanish undetected by the Empire\n
HAM_DIGITAL_4: The Rebels vanish undetected by the Empire\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 5
/$ 4 HD5 THOR32  @>|
<MODEM:THOR32><GOFREQ:750><TX>\n
HAM_DIGITAL_5: The ghost in the wireless emerges through the static\n
HAM_DIGITAL_5: The ghost in the wireless emerges through the static\n
HAM_DIGITAL_5: The ghost in the wireless emerges through the static\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 6
/$ 5 HD6 FELDHELL @>|
<MODEM:FELDHELL><GOFREQ:1400><TX>\n
HAM_DIGITAL_6: WHAT IN THE HELLSCHREIBER IS THIS NOISE\n
HAM_DIGITAL_6: WHAT IN THE HELLSCHREIBER IS THIS NOISE\n
HAM_DIGITAL_6: WHAT IN THE HELLSCHREIBER IS THIS NOISE\n
<RX>

